      "text_helper": "Section 11.12.5 \"ADC sample time register 2 (ADC_SMPR2)\" in chapter 11 (Analog-to-digital converter (ADC)), RM0008 Rev 21, page 245.",
      "section_content": "Address offset: 0x10\nReset value: 0x0000 0000\nBits 31:30 Reserved, must be kept at reset value.\nBits 29:0 SMPx[2:0]: Channel x Sample time selection\nThese bits are written by software to select the sample time individually for each channel.\nDuring sample cycles channel selection bits must remain unchanged.\n000: 1.5 cycles\n001: 7.5 cycles\n010: 13.5 cycles\n011: 28.5 cycles\n100: 41.5 cycles\n101: 55.5 cycles\n110: 71.5 cycles\n111: 239.5 cycles\nNote: ADC3 analog input Channel9 is connected to VSS.",
